164df321a11fa37e03c1309bd8ec65a37d50c5dd220f3a65f910ab03&node=scalar.conditional_rounding&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=7606ede1164df321a11fa37e03c1309bd8ec65a37d50c5dd220f3a65f910ab03&view=arguments&node=scalar.conditional_rounding&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=7606ede1164df321a11fa37e03c1309bd8ec65a37d50c5dd220f3a65f910ab03&ref=sha256%3A3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db%2Fnodes%2Fscalar.conditional_rounding","record":{"assumption_ids":["scalar.paper_admissible"],"boundary":"This is a conditional expectation identity, not a claim that F_N equals the terminal gradient pointwise. Independence and the bound |u|≤1 are essential.","citation_ids":["scalar-r2-26-cite-conditional-rounding"],"evidence_ids":[],"id":"scalar.conditional_rounding","kind":"claim","label":"Independent Gaussian rounding preserves the conditional mean","locator":"consequences.tex:107–115,162–170; rounding paragraph","source_id":"scalar-r2-26-source-consequences","statement":"For fixed 0<T<1,N with finite positive normalizers, define F_N=sgn(u(T,Y_N)+2 Φ_G(Z_{N+1})−1), with Z_{N+1} independent of the first N coordinates and |u|≤1. Then E[F_N|Z₁,…,Z_N]=u(T,Y_N). Its zero set has probability zero, so the value assigned by sign at zero is immaterial.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/nodes/scalar.conditional_rounding","relations":[{"derived":true,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/nodes/scalar.conditional_rounding","id":"field:4a41526fb2f0b968f70bf9db54f248347e048244adfc3450196eadb88b1ea026","kind":"assumption_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/nodes/scalar.conditional_rounding","semantic_class":"explicit_assumption_reference","source_field":"assumption_ids","to":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba